ving most of the acclaim was his female counterpart,  " [:a {:href "/athletes/64506"} "Betty Cuthbert"] ", of the host nation, who duplicated his feat in winning three gold medals. " [:a {:href "/athletes/77531"} "Vladimir Kuts"] " of the USSR won the first gold medal for a male athlete from that nation, doubling in the 5 and 10K. On the field " [:a {:href "/athletes/78857"} "Al Oerter"] " won the first of four consecutive gold medals in the discus throw. His teammate, " [:a {:href "/athletes/78255"} "Hal Connolly"] ", won the hammer throw in a highly anticipated battle against Soviet " [:a {:href "/athletes/77514"} "Mikhail Krivonosov"] ", who placed second. During the 1956 Olympics, Connolly also met Czech discus thrower " [:a {:href "/athletes/77826"} "Olga Fikotová"] ", and they began a romance that ended with them marrying later in 1957. " [:a {:href "/athletes/76736"} "Emil Zátopek"] " served as best man at the wedding in Praha."] "\n\n"] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "Events"] "\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped"} "\n" [:thead {} "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Event"] "\n" [:th {} "Status"] "\n" [:th {} "Date"] "\n" [:th {} "Participants"] "\n" [:th {} "NOCs"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/59241"} "100 metres, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "23 – 24 November 1956"] "\n" [:td {} "65"] "\n" [:td {} "31"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/59264"} "200 metres, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "26 – 27 November 1956"] "\n" [:td {} "67"] "\n" [:td {} "32"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/59287"} "400 metres, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "28 – 29 November 1956"] "\n" [:td {} "43"] "\n" [:td {} "23"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/59306"} "800 metres, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "23 – 26 November 1956"] "\n" [:td {} "38"] "\n" [:td {} "24"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/59317"} "1,500 metres, Men"]] "\n